menu "Air purifier"

config PURIFIER_DEVICE_NAME
    string "Device name"
    default ""
    help
        Name this purifier shows in Matter controllers (Basic Information
        NodeLabel), at most 32 bytes. Empty: "Air Purifier 3H" or
        "Air Purifier 3C", from the detected model. Give each unit its own
        name, e.g. "Bedroom purifier".

config PURIFIER_SETUP_DISCRIMINATOR
    int "Pairing discriminator (0-4095)"
    range 0 4095
    default 2250
    help
        12-bit number in the pairing code that lets a controller find this
        unit. Units that may be paired at the same time need different
        values.

config PURIFIER_SETUP_PASSCODE
    int "Pairing passcode (1-99999998)"
    range 1 99999998
    default 79983961
    help
        The secret part of the pairing code. Give each unit its own. Trivial
        values (12345678, 11111111, ...) are rejected at build time. The
        firmware derives the matching SPAKE2+ verifier at boot, and prints
        the resulting QR payload and manual code on the console.
        The serial number shown in controllers is a separate setting:
        Component config > CHIP Device Layer > Device Identification Options.

config PURIFIER_OTA_TOKEN
    string "Update token"
    default ""
    help
        If set, a firmware update over Wi-Fi (HTTP POST to /ota) must carry
        the header "Authorization: Bearer <token>". Empty lets anyone on the
        network update the purifier.

endmenu
